Command-line tools

Install:
  Install missing APT packages and isolated Python tools; prepare uv and the user command PATH as needed.

Upgrade:
  Update installed command-line packages, uv and isolated uv tools.

Status:
  Report installed versions by purpose and show available APT versions from the local package index.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  GitHub CLI uses its official APT repository when a source is needed; existing repository and key files are preserved.
  Missing uv is installed in ~/.local/bin; uv manages each Python tool in an isolated environment.
  The Python module is not required; uv selects or downloads the interpreters needed by its tools.
  Open a new terminal after installation to load PATH changes.
